// tokio-postgres 0.7 (exact):
//   Transaction<'_> has query_opt(sql, params) -> Result<Option<Row>, Error> and
//   execute(sql, params) -> Result<u64, Error> (both async). There is NO begin,
//   commit or rollback method used on Tx: the boundary belongs to in_tx.
//   row.get::<usize, T>(0) -> T where T: for<'a> FromSql<'a>.
// tokio::runtime::Handle::block_on(&self, future) drives a future to completion
// from synchronous code; it is legal here ONLY because PgSession::in_tx runs the
// closure inside tokio::task::block_in_place on a multi-thread runtime.

